  "id": "COMPOUND:40732 - PROTEIN:5841",
  "verbalization": "Justicidin A is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which is in turn targeted by (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and 10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one, all of which ultimately target A-431. This suggests a complex network of interactions where Justicidin A acts as a starting point in a cascade of targets leading to A-431. The evidence supports a mechanism where Justicidin A may influence SNU-387, which in turn affects A-431 through multiple intermediate compounds. The shared targeting of A-431 by these intermediates implies a potential role for Justicidin A in modulating the activity of these compounds, possibly through direct or indirect interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central node in the relationship between Justicidin A and A-431.",
